---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.astro';
import { REBATE_PATH, REBATE_DATE, AFTER_REBATE_PATH, COMPARE_PATH, HOLIDAY_PATH, blackFridayPath, cyberMondayPath, LOOKUP_PATH } from '../../lib/paths';
import { rebateFaqs } from '../../lib/tool-faqs';
import { REBATE_OFFERS, OUTSIDE_OFFERS, UNVERIFIED_NOTES } from '../../lib/rebates-2026';
import { SRC, lineOf } from '../../lib/guides';
import { hasLine, lineUrl, siteBrands } from '../../lib/data';
import { CONTACT_ENABLED, SITE_NAME } from '../../lib/site';
const title = 'November and December 2026 Tire Rebates';
const description = 'Manufacturer rebate windows for November and December 2026, each dated from the maker’s own page. No invented prices or shipping cutoffs.';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Tire rebates', href: REBATE_PATH }];
const faqs = rebateFaqs;
const sourceIds = [...new Set([
  ...REBATE_OFFERS.flatMap((o) => [o.sourceId, ...(o.alsoSourceIds ?? [])]),
  ...OUTSIDE_OFFERS.flatMap((o) => o.sourceIds),
  ...UNVERIFIED_NOTES.map((o) => o.sourceId),
])];
const sources = sourceIds.map((id) => SRC[id]);
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) }];
const brandHref = (slug: string) => siteBrands.some((b) => b.slug === slug) ? `/tires/${slug}/` : '';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} crumbs={crumbs} ld={ld} published={REBATE_DATE} modified={REBATE_DATE}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Tool · buying dates</p>
  <h1>Tire rebate lookup: November and December 2026</h1>
  <p class="guide-meta"><span>By {SITE_NAME}</span><span>Last updated <time datetime={REBATE_DATE}>{REBATE_DATE}</time></span></p>
  <div class="answer">The maker pages below state a purchase window that includes November 2026. They were read on {REBATE_DATE}. They do not use the words Black Friday or Cyber Monday. November 27 and November 30, 2026 fall inside those windows. None of them states a December 2026 purchase window. December dates below are submission deadlines, and Pirelli’s terms PDF prints two different deadlines. No page we read states a cutoff for shipping the tires. Amounts are the makers’ words. This site does not fill in a tire price.</div>
  <p>The two calendar days have their own pages: <a href={blackFridayPath}>Black Friday, November 27, 2026</a> and <a href={cyberMondayPath}>Cyber Monday, November 30, 2026</a>. They use these same windows. They do not add a sale price. The rest of the exact-match list is on <a href={LOOKUP_PATH}>exact tire lookups</a>.</p>

  <section class="calc" aria-labelledby="reb-h">
    <h2 id="reb-h">Look up a November or December purchase window</h2>
    <p>The table is only the offers whose purchase dates include a day in November or December 2026. A missing brand means we did not verify a window from that maker’s page. It does not mean a store is barred from its own sale.</p>
    <form class="calc-form" onsubmit="return false">
      <label>Purchase or submission month
        <select id="rb-when">
          <option value="2026-11">Purchase window includes November 2026</option>
          <option value="2026-12">Purchase window includes December 2026</option>
          <option value="submit-12">Maker prints a December 2026 submission date</option>
          <option value="all">All verified November–December purchase windows</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Maker or tire name<input id="rb-q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="for example Michelin" /></label>
    </form>
    <p id="rb-empty" class="meta" hidden>No verified offer matches that filter. A December purchase window was not on any manufacturer page we read.</p>
    <div class="tw"><table id="rb-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Offer</th><th>Purchase dates on the page</th><th>Submission date on the page</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {REBATE_OFFERS.map((o) => {
          const src = SRC[o.sourceId];
          return <tr data-months={o.purchaseMonths.join(' ')} data-submit={o.decemberSubmission ? 'submit-12' : ''} data-q={`${o.maker} ${o.name} ${o.tires}`.toLowerCase()}>
            <td><a href={`#${o.id}`}>{o.maker}: {o.name}</a></td>
            <td>{o.purchase}</td>
            <td>{o.submission}</td>
            <td><a href={src.url} rel="noopener">{src.label}</a></td>
          </tr>;
        })}
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <h2>What each page says</h2>
  {REBATE_OFFERS.map((o) => {
    const srcs = [o.sourceId, ...(o.alsoSourceIds ?? [])].map((id) => SRC[id]);
    const brand = brandHref(o.brandSlug);
    const lineLinks = o.lines.map((k) => lineOf(k)).filter((l) => l && hasLine(l));
    return <section id={o.id}>
      <h3>{o.maker}: {o.name}</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Purchase:</strong> {o.purchase}</li>
        <li><strong>Submission:</strong> {o.submission}</li>
        <li><strong>What the page says you get:</strong> {o.reward}</li>
        <li><strong>Tires named:</strong> {o.tires}</li>
        {o.notes.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>Source: {srcs.map((s, i) => <span>{i > 0 ? '; ' : ''}<a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.label}</a> ({s.publisher}, retrieved {s.retrieved})</span>)}.{brand ? <span> Brand grades on this site: <a href={brand}>{o.maker}</a>.</span> : null}</p>
      {lineLinks.length > 0 && <p>NHTSA lines that match a model named above and have a page here: {lineLinks.map((l, i) => <span><a href={lineUrl(l!)}>{l!.brand} {l!.line}</a>{i < lineLinks.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}</span>)}. The treadwear grade on those pages is not a mileage number and is not a rebate.</p>}
    </section>;
  })}

  <h2>Read, and not a November or December purchase</h2>
  <p>These maker pages state a purchase window that ends before November 2026. They are not in the lookup table. The claim dates are printed so an October purchase is not confused with a November one.</p>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Maker</th><th>What the page says</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {OUTSIDE_OFFERS.map((o) => <tr>
        <td>{o.maker}</td>
        <td>{o.summary}</td>
        <td>{o.sourceIds.map((id, i) => { const s = SRC[id]; return <span>{i > 0 ? '; ' : ''}<a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.label}</a></span>; })}</td>
      </tr>)}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Pages that did not state a November or December 2026 offer</h2>
  <ul>
    {UNVERIFIED_NOTES.map((o) => {
      const s = SRC[o.sourceId];
      return <li><strong>{o.maker}.</strong> {o.summary} <a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.label}</a>.</li>;
    })}
  </ul>
  <p>A brand that is not named here was not added. If the maker’s page could not be read, this site skips that row rather than guessing a date or an amount.</p>

  <h2>Use the amount with your own quote</h2>
  <p>Type the rebate from the maker’s page, or from your receipt, on the <a href={AFTER_REBATE_PATH}>cost per mile after rebate</a> calculator. The box stays empty until you type it. The same formula without a rebate is on <a href={COMPARE_PATH}>compare two tires by cost per mile</a>. Winter gear, still without a shipping cutoff, is in the <a href={HOLIDAY_PATH}>holiday 2026 gift guide</a>.</p>
  <p>{CONTACT_ENABLED ? <span>A correction to a date on this page goes through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</span> : <span>How to send a correction is described on <a href="/about/">About</a>.</span>} The byline is {SITE_NAME}.</p>

  <FaqList faqs={faqs} />
  <section class="sources" aria-labelledby="src-h"><h2 id="src-h">Sources</h2>
    <ol>{sources.map((s) => <li><a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.label}</a>, {s.publisher}. <span class="why">Retrieved {s.retrieved}.</span></li>)}</ol>
    <p class="why">Found an error? See <a href="/about/">About &amp; corrections</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
<script is:inline>
(function () {
  var when = document.getElementById('rb-when');
  var q = document.getElementById('rb-q');
  var empty = document.getElementById('rb-empty');
  var rows = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#rb-table tbody tr'));
  function apply() {
    var mode = when.value;
    var needle = (q.value || '').toLowerCase().trim();
    var shown = 0;
    rows.forEach(function (row) {
      var months = row.getAttribute('data-months') || '';
      var submit = row.getAttribute('data-submit') || '';
      var hay = row.getAttribute('data-q') || '';
      var monthOk = mode === 'all' || mode === '2026-11' || mode === '2026-12' ? (mode === 'all' ? true : months.indexOf(mode) !== -1) : submit === mode;
      if (mode === 'all') monthOk = true;
      var textOk = !needle || hay.indexOf(needle) !== -1;
      var on = monthOk && textOk;
      row.hidden = !on;
      if (on) shown++;
    });
    empty.hidden = shown !== 0;
  }
  when.addEventListener('change', apply);
  q.addEventListener('input', apply);
})();
</script>
